NAME: Weekend plan
OWNER: Life Concierge
ACCOUNT: personal
WHEN: Thursdays at 2:00 PM (Eastern)
MILESTONE: M5
STATUS: Created paused. Turned on only after Chris says yes.
---
Switch check: read /workspace/chris-personal/context/routines-on.md. If "Weekend plan" isn't listed there as "on" or "test", append "<time ET> · Weekend plan · SKIPPED_OFF" to /workspace/chris-personal/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md and stop.
Test mode: if it's listed as "test", send every message to Chris only, never to a channel or anyone else, and start each message with "TEST".
Isolation guard: work only in /workspace/chris-personal/ and this account's connected apps. If /workspace/chris-personal/context/owner.md is missing, append "<time ET> · Weekend plan · NO_CLIENT_SOURCE" to the run log and stop. Never use another bot's files, logins or memory.
Lean run: read only what this job needs. If nothing changed, append "<time ET> · Weekend plan · NO_CHANGE" to the run log and stop.
Run log: when you finish, append "<time ET> · Weekend plan · EXECUTED · <one-line result>" to /workspace/chris-personal/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md, or FAILED with the reason. A source you couldn't read is UNKNOWN in your output, never zero.

Use the life-planning skill, section Weekend plan. Check where Chris is: the "Where I am" line in /workspace/chris-personal/context/owner.md. If it's missing or more than 7 days old, plan for the last city you know and open the message with "Planning for <city>. Wrong city? Tell me." Never wait for an answer.
Find and verify three options for that city (one big night, one easy night, one daytime thing), each with day and local time, price level, a reservation link and a backup. Skip anything in /workspace/chris-personal/vault/Life/Never-again.md and anything that clashes with his personal calendar.
Send them in one phone-short message ending "Reply 1, 2, 3 or 'more like 2'." Log the plan in /workspace/chris-personal/vault/Life/Plans.md. Book, reserve and buy nothing. If any personal routine that was due this week has no line in /workspace/chris-personal/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md, add one line at the end: "<routine> didn't run: paused? Check its Details tab."
